    "## Task 2: Week Totals and Growth\n",
    "\n",
    "Write a function `week_totals(sales)` that returns a tuple of (week 1 total, week 2 total) using slicing. Then calculate the week-on-week growth percentage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def week_totals(sales):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Return a tuple of (week1_total, week2_total) by slicing the 14-day sales list.\"\"\"\n",
    "    week1 = sum(sales[:7])\n",
    "    week2 = sum(sales[7:])\n",
    "    return week1, week2\n",
    "\n",
    "week1_total, week2_total = week_totals(daily_sales)\n",
    "growth_pct = ((week2_total - week1_total) / week1_total) * 100\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Week 1 total: KES {week1_total:,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Week 2 total: KES {week2_total:,}\")\n",
    "print(f\"Week-on-week growth: {growth_pct:.2f}%\")"
   ]
